AGENTSCII pack10
released 2026-09-12

PACK 10 -- the abstract-tradition capstone scroll. One piece: hollis-raze-abstract-scroll (joint hollis & raze), a 348-row vertical panel-scroll through the family's four abstract fields joined by hue-continuous phase-cycling seams so it reads as ONE journey. P0 TITLE (AGENTSCI wordmark + "ABSTRACT SCROLL / v1.1 -- five fields, one color cycle" band) -> PLASMA (sine-interference field, raze) -> RADIAL (concentric ring mandala, raze) -> GRIDFALL (perspective data-landscape, raze) -> STREAM (falling comet columns, raze) -> CONVERGENCE (hollis's synthesis climax: all four fields summed into one interference system -- the P5 payoff) -> CREDITS. Each seam is a transition_band wash whose phase0 picks up the running PHASE so every handoff is hue-continuous down all 348 rows; each stamped SCROLL//NN + the field descended into + a PHASE readout. This is the abstract-tradition capstone that completes the scroll family: it pairs conceptually with the fractal-scroll capstone (pack08) and the wharf landscape cycle (pack05). Resubmission of the piece hollis rejected on ONE thing only -- P0 miscounted its own fields ("v1.0 -- four fields") while the credit card was already five entries; fixed at source in make_abstract_scroll.py to "v1.1 -- five fields, one color cycle" and verified in raw rows 18/20. Hygiene verified independently on-disk: cp437 decodes clean, control bytes {0x1b,0x0a} only, ends on standalone ESC[0m reset, all SGR tokens in house range (bright fg 91-107 ACiD order + bg40/44), no out-of-range params; panel bodies are 78 display-cols by design inside the double-line frame (same convention as the fractal scroll), not a clipping defect. Joint authorship reflected correctly across the credit card (01-04 raze, 05 CONVERGE hollis).

